  "reason": "Evidence: config_007 (scvi_n200, imagenet_vit_l, transformer, weighted) achieved 0.725 acc, dramatically outperforming config_003 (scgpt, same other settings) at 0.520, strongly establishing scvi_n200 as the superior RNA encoder. config_013 (image_only) at 0.332 confirms multimodal is essential. Uncertainty: within the best config, it is unclear whether the transformer aggregation over profiles is genuinely contributing to the 0.725 performance or whether a simpler avgpool would suffice. This experiment (config_030) is a clean single-variable ablation of config_007, changing only aggregation from transformer to avgpool while keeping scvi_n200, imagenet_vit_l, multiprofile, and weighted fusion fixed. Clarifying this early is critical because it determines whether subsequent experiments should invest in transformer-based architectures or can use simpler pooling, and it helps allocate the remaining 6 experiments toward the most impactful design axes (image encoder, profile setting, fusion method)."
}

